Fixing the production failure — inspecting the incident and repro.
I've confirmed the nested prefix failure — now tracing the prefix joining logic.
I've pinpointed the double-slash bug — now applying the fix.
The main case now passes — running final edge-case validation.
Root cause: `buildRoutePrefix()` in `lib/plugin-override.js` joined nested prefixes incorrectly. When parent prefix ended with `/` (e.g. `/api/`) and child prefix had no leading `/` (e.g. `v1`), it unconditionally prepended `/` to the child, producing `/api//v1`. The route `GET /orders` was then registered at `/api//v1/orders` instead of `/api/v1/orders`, so `GET /api/v1/orders` missed (404 path, surfaced as `E_PREFIX_JOIN` 500 by the app).

Files changed:
- `lib/plugin-override.js:85` — changed `else if (pluginPrefix[0] !== '/')` to `else if (pluginPrefix[0] !== '/' && !instancePrefix.endsWith('/'))`, so a separator `/` is only added when neither side already provides one. The `endsWith('/') && startsWith('/')` dedup branch is unchanged.

Validation:
- `/work/repro`: before `ORIGINAL_FAILURE_REPRODUCED status=500`, after `ORIGINAL_FAILURE_ABSENT status=200`.
- `node --test test/route-prefix.test.js`: 26/26 pass.
- `node --test test/404s.test.js`: 83/83 pass.
- `node --test test/plugin.1.test.js test/plugin.3.test.js test/route.2.test.js`: pass.
- Manual prefix matrix (`/api/`+`v1`, `/api/`+`/v1`, `/api`+`v1`, `/api`+`/v1`, `/`+`v1`, `/`+`/v1`) all resolve to single-slash URL with 200; existing `/v1/`+`/inner/` trailing-slash case still 200.

Remaining uncertainty: full test suite not run; fix assumes prefixes are non-empty strings and only normalizes the join point (no broader trailing-slash normalization).

